{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/815332-2ed-idol","id":815332,"title":"[2ed] Idol","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-24T03:01:33-08:00","id":815332,"title":"[2ed] Idol","content":"Talking about Majesty in a previous post, I would like to point the attention on this particular power.<br /> I really like the idea behind Idol but I think, while it's really useful vs neonates, it's too useless against other elder. This should be the top power of Majesty but Loyalty and Green Eyes are more viable against elder then this one due to the mechanics. I means, an elder would have at least 4-5 dice to roll in order to acts against the Majesty user. He would achieve a success in the 90% of cases.<br /> What about if the power requires the expense of a willpower in order to roll resolve + blood potency to act against the vampire? And also if he succcedes in the roll, what about if he suffers Majesty as penality in any roll (physical and social) made against the Majesty user??","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T03:36:20-08:00","id":815344,"title":"","content":"Majesty is fine as it is right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T06:31:19-08:00","id":815400,"title":"","content":"Majesty as a whole is pretty weak against those with high Blood Potency. Basic Awe can be shrugged of with Predator's Aura. Confidant and Loyalty are already contested with Blood Potency (plus the Indomitable merit). <br /> <br /> Majesty isn't direct Dominate. Its meant to be a subtle crowd-control power, spreading out through a large number of people, used like a scapal. Trying to use it as a blunt force instrument is meant to be a problem. If you want to use it like a hammer, that's what the Cult of Personality devotion is for. And, even then, high BP are resistant to the effect. This is a constant theme throughout the Discipline. I mean, look at the name. <i>Idol</i>. You use your aura to make yourself a figure of adoration that the weak willed are swayed by. Stronger, older figures that know better shrug it off. There's a reason its not called <i>Sovereignty </i>anymore. <br /> <br /> With Majesty, you go through the steps. You need to put in actual effort to use it to the full potential. You walk into the room, you activate Awe. Everyone who sees you catches your eye. Then, you spend time mingling. Go up to everyone, smile. They welcome you into the circle for a bit (because Awe). You spread Confidant around. It doesn't cost vitae. You seed the area, making the ground fertile. For those people you -really- need to impress, you need to spend the time and attention to flatter them with Loyalty. You don't insta-snap the power and enthrall ancients to your whim. That would be too much. That's also the domain of Dominate, and I like the powers not overlapping. <br /> <br /> That said, I don't recommend elders facing down someone with Majesty anyways. Enfeebling Aura means that Daeva are probably going to out muscle even some elders once the rival's own Vigor is stripped away. Someone with Majesty 5, Vigor 5 and Enfeebling Aura can potentially out grapple even an elder; though, much more likely, they'd just stake them - 5 damage is nothing when Enfeebling just ripped away your Resilience; you're dealing 6 damage at minimum at this point.<br /> <br /> In a way, I like comparing Dominate and Majesty to the Invictus and Movement. One's all about direct loyalty and unassailable elders, and the other is spreading out over a large crowd of younger folk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T06:50:17-08:00","id":815413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/815332-2ed-idol?p=815400#post815400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Majesty as a whole is pretty weak against those with high Blood Potency. Basic Awe can be shrugged of with Predator's Aura. Confidant and Loyalty are already contested with Blood Potency (plus the Indomitable merit).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes Loyalty is contested with blood potency but the roll is fair. I mean. Majesty user rolls Manipulation + Empathy + Majesty while opponent resist with Resolve + Blood Potency. It means that the potential dice pool for both can be equal for every level of blood potency. So for a neonates is difficult to entheralls an elder with BP 5 or more...but for an elder the chance rises and become equal to the subject's ones.<br /> This is not true for Idol. This means that a really ancient vampire with BP 10 has the same chance to succesfully use Idol as a BP 5 vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 01-24-2016, 10:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T08:00:04-08:00","id":815454,"title":"","content":"Lets put it this way. Why should Majesty 5 be able to instantly captivate an entire room of elders? Isn't that a little strong? Is it thematic for a BP 1 neonate to enthrall an entire room of people 400 years older than them? Make no mistake, Lashing Out is an offensive action, which Idol would prevent.<br /> <br /> Spending a willpower is meaningless, because that'd be pretty much a given. Major NPCs aren't shy of willpower. <br /> <br /> Taking a penalty to attack? Well, most social &quot;attacks&quot; aren't rolled. I don't need to roll socialize to insult someone. Maybe to see how well its recieved by the audience, but the audience is already pretty much already on the Majesty user's side. Intimidate the user? That's using Hard Leverage and opening Doors - why should having Majesty on make you resistant to being scared? Its not a mental defense ability.<br /> <br /> Penalty to physical attacks? Not a fan of the overlap with Celerity, which is the Defense raising power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 01-24-2016, 11:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T08:14:45-08:00","id":815464,"title":"","content":"Also, consider this. If it comes to being attacked while you have Idol up by an elder.... you can bet they'll be Riding the Wave. Someone Riding the Wave is all but immune to mind effects when in frenzy.<br /> <br /> Daeva are my favorite clan, and to be honest? I like the Serpents needing to be smart with their powers.<br /> <br /> EDIT - Actually, let me ask this too. Why does <i>Idol</i> need to affect elders easily? What is the purpose? Other than making it more powerful? Does it make better stories? Plot you have in mind?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 01-24-2016, 11:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T11:23:22-08:00","id":815582,"title":"","content":"Well but I didn't mean easily. I just noticed that, all other mental disciplines, have a fair probability to works. A newbie vampire would have low probabilities to &quot;control&quot; an elder becouse of hig blood potency, while an elder could have the same chance or at least the same dice number to roll. With Idol this not happen. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T14:39:46-08:00","id":815694,"title":"","content":"But that's just it. They're all pretty limited in some way. Dominate needs eye contact. Majesty has strength-of-will issues. Obfuscate works pretty well at hiding you from anyone, no roll needed of any kind, but you're FUBAR when it comes to technology. Auspex's telepathy can project thoughts, but not really control. Animalism 4 Feral Infection isn't eactly difficult to resist either - may not be Blood Potency, but still less likely as the vamp ages - and even then, its undirected frenzy. Nightmare causes hallucinations - its a glorified illusion ability now, mixed with Dementation. You can shrug it off most of it with willpower, Lashing out against offensive images, or just Riding the Wave. <br /> <br /> Of the six &quot;mental&quot; disciplines, Dominate and Obfuscate are the only one that's most likely to succeed on an elder. You succeed on that first Mesmerize power, everything else is cake walk. Obfuscate, much like Animalism 4, has a few rolls that you subtract your Discipline rating from. Everything else relies on being tricky and smart with your powers. <br /> <br /> Honestly, the only difference between Idol's roll and Feral Infection or Touch of Shadow's rolls is that Blood Potency can rise beyond 5, while even an elder is unlikely raises their attributes that high even with BP 6+. And if you use a power on an elder, you can expect a large dice pool, no matter if we talk Resolve+Composure or Wits+Composure. And likely some merits as well to boost those rolls higher. I think we're pretty consistant here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T14:58:34-08:00","id":815702,"title":"","content":"I do like that Idol isn't the get out of combat free card that Soverignty was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T20:55:27-08:00","id":815873,"title":"","content":"Idol has saved my ass in combat a couple of times.. Say you ( and likely your party ) get into a room with a few neonates and maybe an elder ... Shit goes down.. You take your time awe, charm a couple. Then reflexively hit of idol and all those neonates the elder thought he has will now take a bullet to save your ass, risk their lives. Strength in numbers... <br /> <br /> Or just don't let it get to combat. Idol can be subtle remember, with this and the flavor text why would they WANT to harm you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T02:48:17-08:00","id":815980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/815332-2ed-idol?p=815873#post815873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or just don't let it get to combat. Idol can be subtle remember, with this and the flavor text why would they WANT to harm you?</div> </div> </div> </div>I always seen Awe as subtle, and growing up with the levels power I've been thinking about Majesty effect as a wrecking ball that smash your feeling <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I really like this concept. Also, Idol's descriptions talks about this power as enhancing Awe's Aura to DIVINE (or blasphemous) level. I don't see it too much subtle :P<br /> Furthermore, when I talk about this power I do not mean just in combat situation <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> A &quot;Social&quot;elder NPC that get into elysyum, or join to a debate, for any reason, at the presence of other elders...less &quot;socially oriented&quot;, and during it become subject to insults of an harpy (or other contradictions). So she acrtive Idol and for the rest of the scene the harpy shuts under the weight of the elder aura...and every word the harpy (or other elders) wants to utter to contradict the DIVINE BEING in the room, costs a lot of fatigue and the most parts of them remains choked in her trhoat.<br /> Mind you, I'm talking about elder vs elder SOCIAL FIGHT. I definitively do not want a neonates or even ancilla, get this result against an elder. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 01-25-2016, 05:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T05:43:07-08:00","id":816035,"title":"","content":"You're already swaying a crowd, which is a huge advantage in any social-style combat situation (I'd use the Chase rules system myself). The whole point of social combat in your given scenario isn't to convince the elder. You're convincing the crowd - which Awe's bonuses and the charming effect of Idol have already done. You are already getting +5 dice to any social attempt here. Idol's already firmly pushed the majority of the crowd on your side, which I imagine could be another bonus. <br /> <br /> And now, you want more? It just seems excessive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}